# 3. CORE UX & MICRO-INTERACTION RULES

- **Responsive by default:** fluid sizing, breakpoints per 1.4, zero horizontal overflow.
- **Smooth animations:** `transition: var(--transition-normal) var(--ease-standard)` on all state changes; fully disabled under `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`.
- **Accessibility (a11y):** semantic HTML5 landmarks (`header`, `nav` with `aria-label`, `main`, `footer`), one `h1`, logical heading order, full keyboard operability, visible focus everywhere, `aria-live` for all dynamic feedback, ≥ 4.5:1 contrast in both modes, and **never color alone** to communicate state (pair error/success colors with icons + text).
- **Mandatory visual feedback:** every click, hover, and submission produces a visible state change.
- **Anchors:** smooth in-page scrolling (respecting reduced motion) with `scroll-margin-top` on sections to clear the sticky nav.
- **Optional:** IntersectionObserver reveal animations (opacity/translate) — guarded by reduced-motion and fully visible when JS is absent.

